.TH ARX 1 2026-11-13 "Arx 0.0.9rc2" "Arx manual"
.SH NAME
arx \- autonomous defensive security agent for Linux servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arx
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B arx shell
.br
.B arx \-\-help
|
.B arx
.I command
.B \-\-help
|
.B arx \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Arx learns what is normal on a server, notices what does not belong and contains it on its own,
with actions it can undo. Anything irreversible waits for the owner's authorization word.
.PP
Arx starts in observe mode: it reports what it would do and changes nothing outside its own files.
Automatic responses need
.BR \-\-enforce .
.PP
Life cycle:
.B setup
\(->
.B recon
\(->
.B learn
\(->
.BR guard .
Most commands need root.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Setting up
.TP
.BR "setup " [ \-\-show ]
Configuration wizard: language, model providers (optional), authorization word, scope, baseline
window, license, alerts, automatic response, improvement program.
.B \-\-show
prints the configuration with secrets redacted.
.TP
.BR "recon " [ "\-\-json \fIpath\fP" ] " " [ \-\-no\-save ]
Read-only map of the host: hardware, packages, services, ports, users, SUID, cron, network.
Saves the inventory as JSON unless
.BR \-\-no\-save .
.TP
.BR "learn " [ "\-\-samples \fIn\fP" ] " " [ "\-\-interval \fIs\fP" ] " " [ \-\-seal ] " " [ \-\-status ]
Take snapshots of normal behavior and merge them into the baseline. Repeat over a few days, then
.B \-\-seal
to close it (also backs up critical files and loads Arx's nftables table).
.TP
.BR "guard " [ \-\-enforce ] " " [ "\-\-interval \fIs\fP" ] " " [ \-\-once ] " " [ \-\-verbose ] " " [ \-\-chat ]
Watch, detect and respond in the foreground. Sweeps every 30 seconds by default.
.B \-\-enforce
applies automatic, reversible Tier 1 actions.
.B \-\-chat
talks to the configured model; it cannot act.
.TP
.BR "service install " [ \-\-enforce ] " " [ "\-\-exec \fIpath\fP" ] | " uninstall" | " status"
Run Arx 24/7 under systemd (arx.service, arx-firewall.service, arx-down.service,
arx-revive.timer, arx-maintenance.slice).
.SS Day to day
.TP
.BR "status " [ \-\-json ]
How things stand: baseline, mode, watchers, blocks, findings, pending actions, recent incidents.
.TP
.BR "accept " [ \fIid\fP ] " " [ \-\-dir | \-\-children ]
Without an id, list findings that can be accepted. With one, add it to the baseline and lift what
contained it.
.B \-\-dir
accepts a service's program directory;
.B \-\-children
also what that program starts.
.TP
.BR "authorize " [ \fIid\fP ]
List pending Tier 2 actions, or carry one out after asking for the authorization word.
.TP
.BR "unblock " [ \fIip\fP | \fIid\fP ]
List temporary blocks, or lift one now (word).
.TP
.BR "unlock " [ \fIaccount\fP ]
List accounts Arx locked, or unlock one (word). Locked accounts never unlock on their own.
.TP
.BR "restore " [ \fIid\fP ]
List quarantined files, or put one back (word).
.SS Tools
.TP
.BR "canaries plant " [ "\-\-in \fIdir\fP" "]... | " list " | " check
Plant, list or check decoy files. Default locations: each user's home and /root.
.TP
.BI "scan " path
Static analysis of a file; it is never run. Exit status 0 means no rule matched.
.TP
.BR "forensics " [ "\-\-since \fIiso\fP" ] " " [ "\-\-verify \fIpath\fP" ] " " [ \-\-indicators ]
Sealed incident report, saved in /var/lib/arx/forensics/.
.B \-\-indicators
prints only public IPs, hashes and attack types.
.TP
.BR "vaccines " [ list " | " update " | " "remove \fIid\fP" ]
Signed vaccines learned by other Arx hosts, validated locally before they apply.
.TP
.BR "proposals " [ list " | " "apply \fIid\fP" " | " "revert \fIid\fP" ]
Changes Arx suggests. Nothing applies without the word.
.TP
.BR "metrics " [ "\-\-days \fIn\fP" ] " " [ \-\-json ]
Noise on this host: high alerts, false positives, unreviewed alerts.
.B \-\-json
holds only numbers.
.TP
.B notify test
Send a test message through every configured alert channel.
.TP
.BR "telemetry " [ status " | " show " | " enable " | " disable " | " send ]
Improvement program: anonymous usage reports, sent only after the owner says yes.
.B show
prints exactly what would be sent.
.TP
.BR "license activate \fIKEY\fP" " | " status " | " deactivate
Pro/Business license. Core needs none.
.TP
.BR "fleet enroll \-\-console \fIURL\fP \-\-token \fITOKEN\fP" " | " status " | " sync
Fleet console (Business).
.TP
.B shell
Interactive console (see below).
.SH CONSOLE
.B arx shell
opens a prompt
.IR user @ host : dir " arx\[u203A]"
where the user is blue, the directory green and typed text yellow. Arx commands are typed without
the leading
.BR arx .
Tab completes commands, actions, options and paths. History is kept in
.IR ~/.arx_history .
Built-ins:
.BR help ", " cd ", " pwd ", " history ", " clear ", " exit .
A failing command never closes the console. Without a terminal it reads one command per line from
standard input.
.SH COLORS
On a terminal Arx colors user names blue, commands yellow and paths green. Only its own output, and
never when writing to a pipe, a file, the journal, Telegram or a webhook. The shell's configuration
is not touched.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARX_LANG
Output language,
.B en
or
.BR es .
.TP
.B ARX_COLOR
.B always
or
.BR never .
Default: colors only on a terminal.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set and not empty, no colors.
.TP
.BR ARX_TELEMETRY=off ", " DO_NOT_TRACK=1
Switch the improvement program off whatever the configuration says.
.TP
.BR ARX_OPENAI_API_KEY ", " ARX_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " ARX_KIMI_API_KEY
Model keys, without writing them to disk.
.TP
.BR ARX_CONFIG_DIR ", " ARX_STATE_DIR
Other configuration and state directories.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/arx/
Configuration and secrets (root, 0600).
.TP
.I /var/lib/arx/
State: baseline, incidents.jsonl, findings, vault, forensics, watch.json.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/arx/arx.pyz
The program.
.TP
.I ~/.arx_history
Console history.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the command did what was asked; 1 when it could not or the answer is negative (wrong word,
file not clean, nothing sent); 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo arx setup
sudo arx recon
sudo arx learn            # repeat over a few days
sudo arx learn \-\-seal
sudo arx service install  # observe mode, 24/7
sudo arx status
sudo arx accept           # list what can be accepted
sudo arx shell
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR auditd (8),
.BR nft (8)
.PP
Full manual: https://github.com/mperez90/Arx/blob/f1-core-mvp/docs/manual.md
